            <ArticleTitle>Visual hallucinations due to indomethacin: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>263-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Visual hallucinations may be caused by organic cerebral lesions and by drugs including indomethacin. We report here a case of indomethacin-induced visual hallucinations in which a clear description of the phenomenology shows how a complex hallucinatory experience may arise from the relatively non-specific effects of cerebral irritation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
